Ask only for the P-CSCF families the PDN will have

A `DNN=ims` context on an IPv6 PDN that asks for both P-CSCF families is
refused by the CP with MATCH_ALL_RULE_NOT_ALLOWED (2253) -- the same answer it
gives when no URSP rule matched at all, which is why this looked like a network
policy problem for a month. It is not: the request is one the network cannot
answer and the CP never forwards it.

The whole IMS context was compared byte for byte against this modem's own
Android, captured off /proc/sitdump mid-registration. Every other field already
matched -- cid 2, rat 14, apn type 1, pdp 2, apn_types 0x40, version 2,
sd/mapped_sd -1, match_all 1, td_mask DNN, dnn 'ims' -- and `@0xdb` was the one
byte that differed: Android sends 2 where we sent 3.

So derive it from the PDP type everywhere rather than hardcoding it, which is
what the vendor does: v4 asks for 1, v6 for 2, v4v6 for 3. The attach request
follows the same rule, and it matters there too now that the attach APN is the
carrier's own entry rather than the IMS APN -- Fizz attaches IPv4 on 'mobile.bm'
and was asking for v6 proxies it could not be given.

